PatchKnob
==============

PatchKnob is a Windows DAW and modular synthesis environment built around:

- tracker, piano-roll, and timeline sequencing
- sampler instruments with keyzones and per-sample editing
- VST2/VST3 hosting with parameter automation
- a GPU-drawn modular rack with Cardinal/VCV-style bridge modules
- Pure Data and Csound patch nodes
- project save/load for sequences, patch graphs, rack state, instruments, and embedded audio

## Links

- Website: https://patchknob.com
- Source: https://github.com/patchknob/patchknob
- Latest installer: https://github.com/patchknob/patchknob/releases/latest
- Patreon: https://www.patreon.com/cw/patchknob

The Patreon link is for project support, custom builds, and binary downloads.

## Windows Build

Build from an MSYS2 MINGW64 shell or a PowerShell with MSYS2 on `PATH`:

```sh
export PATH="/c/msys64/mingw64/bin:/c/msys64/usr/bin:$PATH"
cmake -S . -B build -G "MinGW Makefiles"
cmake --build build --config Release
./build/PatchKnob.exe
```

The build stages the runtime DLL closure next to the executable in `build/`.

## Installer

Create the NSIS installer with:

```sh
cmake --build build --target nsis_installer --config Release
```

The installer is written to:

```text
build/installer/PatchKnob-0.8.7-Setup.exe
```

## Rack Modules

The app loads rack bridge modules from a `modules/` directory next to the
executable, or from the path in `PATCHKNOB_RACK_MODULE_DIR` for compatibility with
older module builds.

